Description: native Linux music library and player
 Rhythm (Linux) is a local music player for GTK 4. It scans a music folder
 for MP3, AAC/M4A, FLAC, WAV, ALAC and AIFF files, with gapless playback,
 crossfade, an equaliser, ratings, play counts and M3U playlists.
 .
 It also has a read-only view of a connected iPhone (through ifuse and
 libimobiledevice) and can send tracks to a paired phone with KDE Connect.
 .
 Not affiliated with Apple.
